Ali al-Tamimi, director general of the authority, said the project follows directives from the transport ministry to develop the country’s technical and operational capabilities, improve vessel monitoring and tracking, and strengthen maritime security, the ministry said in a statement.
ERBIL, Kurdistan Region of Iraq &ndash; Iraq&rsquo;s Supreme Iraqi Maritime Authority on Tuesday inaugurated a Vessel Traffic Services (VTS) system to monitor ships in Iraqi territorial waters and regulate their entry and departure, as attacks on commercial vessels and disruptions to shipping continue in the Strait of Hormuz.
Tamimi said the system was particularly important given Iraq&rsquo;s geographical position along the Shatt al-Arab and the Persian Gulf, as well as &ldquo;the role of its ports in connecting the national economy to international markets.&rdquo;
